---
title: Overview
description: What E-Sign does, who can use it, where it is found, and who can see and act on each signature request.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

E-Sign sends PDF documents to be signed online. You upload one or more PDFs, add the signers, place a signature field for each signer, and send. Each signer gets one email with one link that covers all of their documents. They sign in the browser, without an account. When everyone has signed, the signed PDF is kept with the request and everyone involved is notified.

## Where E-Sign is found

Select **E-Sign** in the left side bar. The page lists, newest first, the signature requests you sent and the ones sent by people who report to you; a tenant admin sees every request of the firm. The page and has two buttons at the top right:

- **+ New Request** — send documents for signature (see [1 · Send a signature request](/en/e-sign/send-request/)).
- **Email templates** — the wording of the emails that signers and CC recipients receive (see [5 · Email content and templates](/en/e-sign/email-templates/)).

Signature requests are also sent from other parts of Operon. They appear on the same list, and the **Source** column says where each one came from:

| Source | Where it was sent from |
|---|---|
| **E-Sign** | **+ New Request** on this page. |
| **Case** | The signing step of a case, with **Set up e-sign**. |
| **Contract** | A contract on a CRM opportunity. See [CRM · 7 · Send for e-signature](/en/crm/e-signature/). |

A request sent from a case or a contract is followed and changed from there. On the E-Sign page it can be opened and read; renaming and withdrawing are available only for requests sent from the E-Sign menu.

## Who can see and do what

Every user of the firm can open E-Sign and send a request. What each person can do with a request depends on who sent it.

| Person | See the request and its status | Open the documents and the sent emails | Download the signed PDF | Remind, change an email, extend, add or remove CC recipients, rename, withdraw | Confirm the completion date |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **The sender** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| **Tenant admin** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| **A manager above the sender** | Yes | Yes | No | Yes | No |
| **A member of the request's department** | Yes | According to their permission set | According to their permission set | No | No |
| **Anyone else in the firm** | Yes | No | No | No | No |

For a request sent from a case, "the sender" is the case's creator and its current assignee. Buttons that you cannot use are not shown.

The E-Sign list shows a request only to its sender, the managers above the sender and tenant admins. Other people in the table above open the request from its case or contract. A request sent from a case is listed under the person who selected **Set up e-sign**; if the case later gets a new assignee, that person follows the request from the case.

{% screenshot id="e-sign/list-by-request" caption="The E-Sign list: one row per request, with its source, signers, status and sender." /%}

